				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-07-12T07:51:03.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Zing! Yes, clever, funny, but… I put together my own website on my own domain. It’s a one pager with no interactive features, I happened to have hosting included with my pay-for email service (Fastmail), I’m a professional software engineer (though not web developer) and it took me over a week!</p><p>Until building a self-sovereign presence on the web is as easy as signing up for a proprietary service people will keep signing up for proprietary services. And that is entirely rational!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
