			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ratkins\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ratkins</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>Kind of like saying that as long as cooking dinner is harder than ordering takeout, people will order takeout. Which...is true. But cooking is still awesome.</p><p>I feel like the real barrier is hosting. People just really don't want to whip out their credit cards and pay every moth, and GitHub etc are too complicated for people who are just getting started.</p>",
