				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-07-12T15:27:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@smyth\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>smyth</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I don’t think the analogy quite holds. It’s more like that if you just get yourself some tools you can service your own car instead of taking it to the mechanic. Except you can’t, because modern cars are incredibly sophisticated and need expensive tools that require years of training to use properly. It’s entirely rational for people to not bother.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110701839102813729",
			"parentId": "110701814951485635",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@smyth/110701839039339904",
			"author": {
				"name": "Patrick",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@smyth",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-07-12T15:33:30.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ratkins\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ratkins</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>I honestly think that cooking and making a website are more comperable in terms of time spent. The issue is that, when you go to learn to make a site, people try to teach you React or whatever. Then it's like building a car from scratch or whatever.</p><p>People find HTML to be pretty intuitive, and cpanel is not hard once people know to look for it. But the current ecosystem is either for normie service users or full blown devs. There used to be more space in between.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110701903040952704",
			"parentId": "110701839102813729",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ratkins/110701903006858170",
			"author": {
				"name": "Robert Atkins",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ratkins",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-07-12T15:49:46.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@smyth\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>smyth</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> You are *vastly* overestimating the technical competence of average human. Cpanel? Ha! I’m a professional software engineer and my life’s too short to eff about with cPanel.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
